To RAN2 and RAN3 ACTION: SA5 kindly asks RAN2 and RAN3 to provide and feedback and update the specification if it is needed. SA5 also attached the CRs for temporary suspension of trace production in Release 20. When checking these CRs, it was clearly indicated that the procedures for temporary suspension will reuse the current ones, see S5-255588, We have also excerpted some of them, as examples for reference. Here for signalling-based trace suspension, it reused 4.1.4.11 and 4.1.2.15, while for signalling-based MDT suspension, it reused 4.1.3.13 and 4.1.2.17. When checking through all the CR, we could see that, all the operations for deactivation and reactivation just refer to the existing sections. While in these existing sections, taking 4.1.4.11 as example, see below This signalling flow describes the signaling Trace Session deactivation procedure in 5GC, in which CN and NG-RAN are involved, and no additional changes were introduced for the purpose of temporary suspension, i.e. the procedures for detailed operations in CN and RAN for temporary suspension just reuse the existing ones. While in RAN3, there are clear definitions on activation and deactivation in 38.413, see below: This message is sent by the AMF to initiate a trace session for a UE. Direction: AMF NG-RAN node

